    "## MACE for MD computation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "One of the most known examples of GNN is [MACE](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2401.00096), an universal machine learning force field. Using some pretrained models, it would be possible to run an MD computation of diverse systems.\n",
    "\n",
    "This model uses material project data base with DFT (PBE+U) structures (here we are using MACE-MP-0, but other data bases are available as pretrained models).\n",
    "\n",
    "For the sake of the example, we can try to see how does the NaCl the solid melts by going above its fusion temperature and below its ebulition temperature."
   ]
